From: Package maintainers <packages@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] bluetoothd: search layered system configuration paths
Source: https://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/bluetooth/bluez-5.85.tar.xz
Upstream: Not submitted; this is a generic UAPI configuration proposal.

Keep an explicit --configfile path exact. When systemd supplies
CONFIGURATION_DIRECTORY, search every directory in its declared order and do
not fall back outside that explicit list. Otherwise select the first existing
configuration from the administrator, transient, and vendor trees.

Use the same selector for main.conf, both input.conf readers, and
network.conf. An existing empty file therefore masks lower policy.
